# Cloudflare Pages / Netlify static-header rules.
# Astro prerenders API routes to plain static files, so the Content-Type /
# Content-Disposition set in the route handler (src/pages/raw/blog/[slug].md.ts,
# src/pages/sitemap.xml.ts) only reaches the browser if the host is told to
# serve these paths with those headers explicitly — see docs/DECISIONS.md
# 2026-07-13 (Decision 13).

/raw/blog/*.md
  Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
  Content-Disposition: inline

/sitemap.xml
  Content-Type: application/xml; charset=utf-8
